00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.100
The episodes will loosely be inspired by the
comics, because Terminus and the Gareth Villain

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.200
is somewhat of an amalgam of the Chris character,
the Leader of The Hunters and because it's

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.540
largely implied by people bones right here
that the Terminus people are cannibals like

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:48.110
the Hunters. I'm going to suggest you read
or re-read Volume 11 of the comic "Fear The

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:51.520
Hunters" it's basically issues 61 to 66.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.300
If you have read the comics, please use spoiler
tags when talking about the characters and

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.620
what happens during those issues.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:01.690
The episodes will be different, even Kirkman
has told them in the last couple of years

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:06.340
to quote unquote, "Have fun with the comic
stories". And Norman Reedus is huge on the

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:10.210
show, Daryl Dixon is probably the most popular
character on the show next to Andrew Lincoln.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:14.200
And Daryl's not even in the comics, so anything
he does automatically has to be a change in

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.890
the original story.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:22.110
I think it just makes it a fun game for comic
book readers to try and guess what they'll

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:25.310
include and looking for easter eggs.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:29.130
In terms of the big stuff happening, Gimple
said there would be some similar twists in

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:33.580
